ah","also":"","summary":"Uzziah.","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"azariah_385","name":"Azariah","also":"","summary":"High priest in the reign of Uzziah, king of Judah (2 Kings 14:21; 2 Chr. 26:17-20).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[17,20]},{"id":"aaron_1","name":"Aaron","also":"","summary":"The eldest son of Amram and Jochebed, a daughter of Levi (Ex. 6:20). Some explain the name as meaning mountaineer, others mountain of strength, illuminator.","verses":331,"father":"Amram","mother":"Jochebed","v":[18]},{"id":"jotham_1735","name":"Jotham","also":"Joatham","summary":"The son and successor of Uzziah on the throne of Judah. As during his last years Uzziah was excluded from public life on account of his leprosy, his son, then twenty-five years of age, administered for seven years the affairs of the kingdom in his father’s stead (2 Chr. 26:21, 23; 27:1).","verses":20,"father":"Uzziah","mother":"Jerushah","v":[21,23]},{"id":"isaiah_617","name":"Isaiah","also":"Esaias","summary":"The son of Amoz (Isa. 1:1; 2:1), who was apparently a man of humble rank. His wife was called “the prophetess” (8:3), either because she was endowed with the prophetic gift, like Deborah (Judg. 4:4) and Huldah (2 Kings 22:14-20), or simply because she was the wife of “the prophet” (Isa. 38:1).","verses":53,"father":"Amoz","mother":"","v":[22]},{"id":"amoz_240","name":"Amoz","also":"","summary":"Strong, the father of the prophet Isaiah (2 Kings 19:2, 20; 20:1; Isa. 1:1; 2:1). As to his personal history little is positively known.","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[22]}],"places":[{"id":"eloth_375","name":"Eloth","kind":"","lat":29.5285,"lon":35.00573,"summary":"","verses":3,"v":[2]},{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[3,9,15]},{"id":"ashdod_101","name":"Ashdod","kind":"City","lat":31.75604,"lon":34.65606,"summary":"Stronghold, a Philistine city (Josh. 15:47), about midway between Gaza and Joppa, and 3 miles from the Mediterranean. It was one of the chief seats of the worship of Dagon (1 Sam. 5:5).","verses":19,"v":[6]},{"id":"gath_442","name":"Gath","kind":"City","lat":31.69353,"lon":34.84388,"summary":"A wine-vat, one of the five royal cities of the Philistines (Josh. 13:3) on which the ark brought calamity (1 Sam. 5:8, 9; 6:17). It was famous also as being the birthplace or residence of Goliath (1 Sam. 17:4).","verses":32,"v":[6]},{"id":"jabneh_615","name":"Jabneh","kind":"","lat":31.86552,"lon":34.74686,"summary":"Building, (2 Chr. 26:6), identical with Jabneel (Josh. 15:11).","verses":1,"v":[6]},{"id":"gurbaal_498","name":"Gurbaal","kind":"","lat":30.73469,"lon":35.60625,"summary":"Sojourn of Baal, a place in Arabia (2 Chr. 26:7) where there was probably a temple of Baal.","verses":1,"v":[7]},{"id":"egypt_362","name":"Egypt","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":26.4902,"lon":29.8808,"summary":"The land of the Nile and the pyramids, the oldest kingdom of which we have any record, holds a place of great significance in Scripture.","verses":564,"v":[8]},{"id":"angle_66","name":"Angle","kind":"","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"","verses":1,"v":[9]},{"id":"corner_gate_307","name":"corner gate","kind":"Fort","lat":31.77744,"lon":35.23494,"summary":"","verses":5,"v":[9]},{"id":"shephelah_1074","name":"Shephelah","kind":"Region","lat":31.75,"lon":34.75,"summary":"region","verses":6,"v":[10]}],"events":[],"traditions":[],"sources":["JFB","MHCC","Wesley"],"tags":{"bsb":[[3605,5971,5971,3063,3063,3947,5818,1931,8337,8337,1121,1121,4427,4427,4427,4427,8478,8478,8478,1,1,558],[1931,1931,1931,1931,1129,1129,359,7725,7725,3063,3063,3063,310,4428,4428,7901,5973,1,1],[5818,8337,8337,1121,1121,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,4427,3389,3389,2572,8141,517,517,8034,3203,3203,4480,4480,4480,3389],[6213,